# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 131's class, lane recovery-b4, beside
# `fixedbugs-131-a-sigil-before-a-name-is-one-message`. Symptom: the value
# after `@v =` went unread with the two messages at the `@`, so its own
# mistake, the `)` below, waited for a second run. Now the line is read as
# the mutation it spells, and the value's mistake is told beside the sigil's
# one message; the certain fix writes `v @ v + )`, which keeps it.

function main()
    v: i64 @= 0
    v @ v + )  #~ expected_expression expected_expression
    print(v)
